Single connection string form (most hosted Postgres providers give you this):

DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:PORT/DATABASE

Set to false for a local Postgres without SSL. Leave true/unset for most
hosted providers (Supabase, Neon, Railway, RDS, etc.).

PGSSL=true

PORT=5000

--- Admin auth -------------------------------------------------------------
On boot, if this email has no row in the admin table yet, one is created
with a randomly generated password, which gets emailed via Resend.

ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

Long random string used to sign login JWTs. Generate one with:
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"

JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-string
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d

From https://resend.com — used to email the generated admin password.

RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

Must be a verified sender/domain in your Resend account.

RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=admin@yourdomain.com

Only needed if the frontend is on a different origin than the API, so the
auth cookie can be sent/received cross-origin.

FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000